{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda","id":1543998,"title":"Best and Worst By Night (Vtm and VdA)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-16T10:20:18-07:00","id":1543998,"title":"Best and Worst By Night (Vtm and VdA)","content":"Greetings, for those of you who have read the various by nights of VtM and VdA, about the By Nights<br /> <br /> 1 - Which one is the best in your opinion and why, what makes it different from the scenario?<br /> <br /> 2 - Which one did you use for the longest time or modify to better fit into your WoD universe?<br /> <br /> 3 - Which one is the worst or most disappointing and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T11:10:30-07:00","id":1544002,"title":"","content":"Well, the best in my opinion is probably a tie between Cconstantinople by Night and Dark Ages Paris by Night for V20 (this last one wasn't translated into English, unfortunately).<br /> Both have very interesting stories and characters to explore and characters who affect the whole history of Vampire. I've used Constantiniple for the longest time, naturally, as it's much older and has many important vampire characters. One thing I like in particular about these two, besides the characters, is that they tried to kind of run away from the same political struggles that characterize most of the &quot;By Night&quot; books, that is, they present different powers/ideas/creatures that are not found outside of them, I won't give spoilers, but what I mean is &quot;crazy ideas&quot; about powers and things one character can make with this powers, like animating things, etc. As a very experienced ST, I tend to get bored easily, especially after so many years, more than 2 decades of storytelling, so it's always refreshing to seee some &quot;crazy ideas&quot; that offer new venues to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T11:53:14-07:00","id":1544003,"title":"","content":"I remember Chicago and LA being the two we probably used the most back in the day. (In hindsight, I really wish that LA's Anarch revolt had occurred in the late 60s/early 70s rather than the 40s, simply because I feel that Film Noir LA Vampire works way better with the Camarilla in control.)<br /> <br /> The biggest missed opportunity IMO is Berlin. The idea of a single city that has been physically divided for 40+ years and only recently reunited but has two rival Princes and Courts is a really great and unique Vampire setting. And Berlin's fascinating history and culture (especially the music/club subcultures of the 70s and 80s, Cold War spy intrigue of the 60s, the film industry of the 20s, and the 19th century University scene) only add to that. But instead, WW2 is presented as pretty much the only thing of note to have happened, and the book is very much the worse for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T11:56:06-07:00","id":1544004,"title":"","content":"Best set - Constantinople and Jerusalem, great characters and plots<br /> <br /> Disapointing sets - Damascus by night (promise in Veil of Night book) and NY by Night (i done know, the metaplot in Nights of the Profecy (&quot;Siege of Camarilla&quot; set) for my is the best chronicle can be, but never whriten correctly in same book <br /> <br /> Bizzare set - Cairo by night is really strange set","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:11:38-07:00","id":1544005,"title":"","content":"Not gonna really be shaking things up too much with these takes but\u2026<br /> <br /> 1. Chicago by Night really is the gold standard that every other \u2018by Night\u2019 title is compared against. It\u2019s a great time capsule and a great introduction to vampire as a setting and filled with hooks to start playing with at your table. Possibly its main flaw is that it was TOO influential <br /> <br /> 2. This is my most unique take but I\u2019ve got a special fondness for DC by Night. It was one of my first WoD books and I\u2019m from the DC metropolitan area so I\u2019ve got a fondness for the city (it\u2019s far more than just Capital Hill!). The cover is iconic (even if only to me) and makes wonderful use of the Washington monument (or, as I called it as a kid, \u2018the big pencil\u2019) as a gothic landmark. Now that said it\u2019s not perfect. Marcus Vitel is a somewhat gonzo concept but his long lasting popularity speaks for itself. Other than him and his brood though, the rest of the city\u2019s vampires are somewhat shaky. Lots of potential though.<br /> <br /> 3. The one that personally irks me the most is LA by Night because it\u2019s arguably one of the most responsible forces for stunting the development of the Anarch movement and it\u2019s taken a long time for its ideas to be scavenged into something useful on these forums. The objectively worse one though, in my opinion, has to be Berlin by Night, for the sheer weight of the missed opportunities. (I wouldn\u2019t even mind the vampire snakes if they were done well, but, it is what it is)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:15:51-07:00","id":1544006,"title":"","content":"Best? Chicago By Night 1st Edition<br /> <br /> Worst? Chicago By Night 5th Edition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:20:26-07:00","id":1544007,"title":"","content":"This might be controversial to some but I actually think there\u2019s a lot of stuff in Chicago by Night V5 that\u2019s worth considering. Even if one isn\u2019t running V5, the way that characters are presented with potential story hooks built into them and clearly identified I think is something useful that I make use of myself from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:24:59-07:00","id":1544008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544005#post1544005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna really be shaking things up too much with these takes but\u2026<br /> 2. This is my most unique take but I\u2019ve got a special fondness for DC by Night. It was one of my first WoD books and I\u2019m from the DC metropolitan area so I\u2019ve got a fondness for the city (it\u2019s far more than just Capital Hill!). The cover is iconic (even if only to me) and makes wonderful use of the Washington monument (or, as I called it as a kid, \u2018the big pencil\u2019) as a gothic landmark. Now that said it\u2019s not perfect. Marcus Vitel is a somewhat gonzo concept but his long lasting popularity speaks for itself. Other than him and his brood though, the rest of the city\u2019s vampires are somewhat shaky. Lots of potential though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long felt that DC would have been the perfect choice for a Vampire/Mage crossover setting sourcebook. For both games you have all of this diverse stuff going on all over the city for PCs to be involved in, while also having the massive sleeping leviathan of the federal government sitting there with DANGER! DO NOT TOUCH! signs slapped all over it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:29:12-07:00","id":1544010,"title":"","content":"One of the things I really liked about Requiem's New Orleans book was how it separated things into Neonate, Ancilla, and Elder levels. I think a lot of the Masquerade by Night books might have benefited from that approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:59:27-07:00","id":1544015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544010#post1544010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I really liked about Requiem's New Orleans book was how it separated things into Neonate, Ancilla, and Elder levels. I think a lot of the Masquerade by Night books might have benefited from that approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Omg I can't like this enough, this is so true! I've ST many elders games during my years of experience and it's a nightmare to have to adapt almost EVERY SINGLE THING in the setting if I want to allow my players to play as elders in a given setting. This would have made my life as a ST much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T16:53:50-07:00","id":1544034,"title":"","content":"I'm not really a fan of these sorts of books in general. I'm generally of the mind of &quot;catch a man a fish, you feed him for a day, teach a man to fish, and you feed him for a lifetime.&quot; City-books are catching the ST a fish. That's basically the source of the idea that Chicago by Night was too influential: the authors didn't really appreciate how much people would treat it as a model of how to do vampire cities instead of an example of one of many ways a city might look. People were, effectively, trying to copy the book's fishing to try to learn how to fish since no book really covered that first.<br /> <br /> So, a bit of a &quot;cheat&quot; of the question, but my favorite city-book is going to remain Damnation City from VtR 1e for sometime because.... it's all about teaching you how to fish. All the others from all the editions and WoD vs. CofD fall into a tie for me otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T18:14:46-07:00","id":1544044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544034#post1544034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> People were, effectively, trying to copy the book's fishing to try to learn how to fish since no book really covered that first.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually chapter three of the 1st edition Storytellers Handbook. Unfortunately, I suspect that the fact that said book never got a 2nd edition (the way the Players Guide did fairly early on) meant that it went overlooked by a lot of people who came in after 1992, and so the by Night books tended to repeat a lot of the Chicago template by default. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T19:02:59-07:00","id":1544057,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'd consider that a real &quot;teach a ST how to build a city.&quot; The entire VtM 1e ST Handbook was 153 pages... one chapter crammed in there is not a lot for something so vital to making a vibrate VtM setting for your home table. Even if you combined all the material in the various VtM ST books, and books like Gilded Cage (which came really late in the original VtM run), it's still less impactful than one book all about providing tools of STs to build custom cities for their games.<br /> <br /> The 1e ST Handbook also came out after CbN 1e... which didn't help the legacy of each book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T19:20:56-07:00","id":1544060,"title":"","content":"It is pretty bare bones, yes, and I think if they had done a 2nd ed STH in 94 or 95, you probably would have been able to do something two or three times the length with a lot more options and suggestions.<br /> <br /> In a more perfect world, I like to imagine that we would have gotten an entire book about the Prince's court and how to design your own, with similar books about Elysium (rather than doubling as an elder sourcebook), the Rack, Domains and Havens, and Primogen councils. <br /> <br /> Also that each by Night book would have tried to be a distinct set up. X is the city with a strong Prince contesting an independent Primogen, Y is the one ruled entirely by the Primogen, Z is the one with just a Prince, and then the two rival courts (Berlin), the group of Anarchs (LA), and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T21:16:49-07:00","id":1544069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544006#post1544006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best? Chicago By Night 1st Edition<br /> <br /> Worst? Chicago By Night 5th Edition</div> </div> </div> </div>5th Edition was awesome.<br /> <br /> A better follow up than 2nd Edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T22:29:05-07:00","id":1544077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda#post1543998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings, for those of you who have read the various by nights of VtM and VdA, about the By Nights<br /> <br /> 1 - Which one is the best in your opinion and why, what makes it different from the scenario?<br /> <br /> 2 - Which one did you use for the longest time or modify to better fit into your WoD universe?<br /> <br /> 3 - Which one is the worst or most disappointing and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Chicago / New Orleans (different STs). Montreal for a Sabbat game.<br /> <br /> 2- New Orleans - ST was a veteran and customized a lot of NPCs<br /> <br /> 3- L.A. But mainly for the ST, his style was not what i was looking for. Anarchs arent my favorite. <br /> <br /> In short, i guess its ST dependent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T22:54:39-07:00","id":1544078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544069#post1544069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5th Edition was awesome.<br /> <br /> A better follow up than 2nd Edition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To each their own, I guess. IMHO, Chicago By Night 5th Edition was terrible by virtue of it being part of the wider 5th Edition setting. <br /> <br /> Chicago By Night 2e wasn't that great either. Tbh, I'd say it was the weakest of the 2e By Night books.<br /> <br /> With that said, I'd say my favorite of the 2e &quot;By Night&quot; books would be Montreal By Night, with LA by Night and Dark Colony tied for second.<br /> <br /> Also, here would be a good &quot;Master List&quot; of setting books for VTM, not counting stuff like France By Night or fan-made content or crossovers with other gamelines (with one very notable exception) like World of Darkness: Hong Kong, Dark Alliance: Vancouver, or Necropolis: Atlanta<br /> <br /> <b>First Edition</b><br /> Alien Hunger (Denver)<br /> Chicago By Night<br /> Milwaukee By Night<br /> A World of Darkness<br /> <br /> <b>Second Edition</b><br /> Chicago by Night: Second Edition<br /> Dark Colony (New England)<br /> L.A. by Night<br /> Berlin by Night<br /> DC by Night<br /> New Orleans by Night<br /> Montreal by Night<br /> A World of Darkness: Second Edition<br /> <br /> <b>Revised Edition</b><br /> San Francisco by Night (KOTE Crossover but was originally planned to be a late 1e/early 2e supplement so I'll include it here)<br /> Mexico City by Night<br /> Cairo by Night<br /> New York by Night<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages and Victorian Age</b><br /> Constantinople by Night<br /> Transylvania by Night<br /> Jerusalem by Night<br /> Iberia by Night<br /> Dark Ages: Europe<br /> Dark Ages: British Isles<br /> London by Night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T23:02:25-07:00","id":1544079,"title":"","content":"I found the books very variable. In my opinion the books go from best to worst as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Top tier</b><br /> <i>Chicago by Night<br /> Constantinople by Night<br /> Transylvania by Night</i><br /> <br /> What puts something in the top tier is that the books present a bigger story about the world than merely the conflict between a group of elders in a given city. All three of the above books were massively influential for how the game developed, and with good reason.<br /> <br /> <b>Well, I Liked It</b><br /> <i>New Orleans by Night</i><br /> <br /> This had some of the best art out of any of these books, a few interesting characters, with enough in the way of interesting and unusual to make them interesting. Nothing to make it truly stand out, but I seem to have liked this more than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <b>Decent Enough</b><br /> <i>DC by Night<br /> Iberia by Night<br /> Mexico City by Night<br /> Milwaukee by Night<br /> New York by Night</i><br /> <br /> These are books that were perfectly fine, but just didn't have anything that interesting to make them stand out.<i> New York by Night </i>managed to be adequate, whilst also being quite boring (which, for a book about New York, was quite a feat).<br /> <br /> <b>Could Do Better</b><br /> <i>Cairo by Night<br /> Berlin by Night<br /> Dark Alliance: Vancouver<br /> Dark Colony<br /> Los Angeles by Night<br /> Montreal by Night</i><br /> <br /> These are books that weren't terrible, but had some significant flaws that should have been worked through in editing. <i>Cairo by Night</i> was rambling (and had at least one historic individual as a vampire, which was supposed to not happen in the revised era). <i>Dark Alliance: Vancouver</i> was developed as a <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i> book, and doesn't quite get kindred society right. Interestingly enough, whilst most people hate <i>Berlin by Night</i>, I don't think it is irredeemable; you could use it as the basis of a decent chronicle with a few tweaks (such as replacing Rasputin, and all the Nazi vampires).<br /> <br /> <b>What Were People Thinking?</b><br /> <i>Jerusalem by Night<br /> London by Night<br /> San Francisco by Night</i><br /> <br /> How can you get a book about Victorian London wrong? Well, London by Night was written by a team of authors who seemed to have no interest in a) London and b) the Victorian era. Terrible maps, (mostly) terrible characters, and a dollop of <i>Mary Poppins</i>. Meanwhile, it would require an entire thread to outline the problems.<br /> <br /> Worst of all, however, is San Francisco by Night which seems to be mired in racist tropes about Asian settlement in California. I don't know why that book didn't earn more opprobrium from readers... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T00:09:33-07:00","id":1544081,"title":"","content":"Given how Requiem's Shadows over Mexico book (also developed by Justin) specifically states that it was aiming for the sort of lurid sensationalism of various films and pop culture rather than any kind of realism, it wouldn't shock me if he had insisted on London by Night being the same. This would also be in line with some of the Dark Ages material like Transylvania by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T04:26:12-07:00","id":1544086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544079#post1544079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Well, I Liked It</b><br /> <i>New Orleans by Night</i><br /> <br /> This had some of the best art out of any of these books, a few interesting characters, with enough in the way of interesting and unusual to make them interesting. Nothing to make it truly stand out, but I seem to have liked this more than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it shows I was a bit distracted when writing this bit\u2026 But one of the nice things is that the book did have a sensible limited number of characters, so we didn\u2019t really end up with unnecessary filler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T05:10:26-07:00","id":1544088,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion, but I actually like having historical and cultural figures as NPC's in these &quot;By Night&quot; books, it adds a certain pulpy charm to it all.<br /> <br /> Fuck, the greatest VTM setting book of all time was chock full of them. Chicago by Night had the likes of Al Capone, Harry Houdini, Mrs. O'Leary, Wat Tyler's girlfriend, and like a quarter of the cast of the friggin' Iliad as elder vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T12:14:17-07:00","id":1544128,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll go on the byzantine train and say that <b>Constantinople by Night</b> is the Chicago by Night of the VtDA books. It offers such a plethora of characters, plots, avenues, tragedies and triumphs, alternate histories and interesting ideas. It also offers a new political system that wasn't present in any other material till then (and ever since). The plot of the Dream is great, and one of the best in the lore, that had amazing repercussions (and is way better than all the Brujah-Carthage stuff that is always mentioned and never explained, and just turns into Baali go birl).<br /> Though I think the V20 Dark Ages Companion sequel is very weak. Basically everything is the same since the 4th crusade, except some new characters that mostly fill old or already-filled roles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages France By Nigh</b>t is also fabulous, and I also regret that is only in French (but I also regret that so many books were never brought to my language). Dark Ages France for vampire is way more interesting than any other area bar Constantinople. Lots of intrigue, mystery, exploration and variety. <br /> <br /> <b>Transylvania By Night</b> is... cool, but it is spread WAY too thin. We have an entire book trying to cover with detail 1/3 of Europe and going only by single characters, instead of structures or societies. And for a book about &quot;Tzimisce land&quot; we get very little Tzimisce in comparison. Almost no Voivodes, surely no content for how the Voivodates work, or examples of Knezes. So cool ideas, but too pulverized for my liking, focusing on characters that many times are unrelated (which should be the basis of any By Night). Showing the Balkans, or just Hungary and Romania should've been more than enough.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I love <b>Dark Ages Europe</b>. The way it presents the regions and princedoms is very concise, and let's each region have a web of relations, alliances and oppositions, instead of a loose gathering of isolated individuals. It advanced a lot of plots, created new scenarios, and gave each of its covered cities and countries good themes. I only wish we had more of it. <br /> <br /> <b>Iberia By Night</b> I thought was hot garbage. It should've been one of the most interesting regions, with Brujah, Toreador, Lasombra and Banu Haqim politics going wild. But it mostly is &quot;Muslisms are Haquimites&quot; and &quot;Christians are Lasombra&quot;, period. There are no freaking Brujah characters to speak of (and even worst, they stick a damn Ventrue as a great general for the Lasombra, out of nowhere), and Toreador basically a passing fad. No plots , just Amicti Noctis deciding &quot;ok, we'll go full-Christian&quot;, and no Banu Haqim putting the Laws of Haqim first (like Ur-Shulgi would many centuries later). There is no theme, no struggle, dilemma or campaign to take part in. It would just turn into War board game, which isn't functional for Vampire (just try the third chapter of Under the Black Cross to see how vampire open-war is very unfun to play). Besides, lots of important Lasombra characters aren't even in the book (like Eliser de Polanco and Tercio Bravo). <br /> <br /> <b>Damascus By Night</b> I agree that is really underwhelming. Nothing in it justifies using Damascus, nor it has anything to do with Ashirra. The plot could've been in any city, and at any era nonetheless. For a book about Ashirra it has very little to do with it, and it does not use a venerable and great city like Damascus with any propriety. It's just the old plot of &quot;degenerate Elder is actually a puppet of a Baali&quot;, which I tire heavily every single time I see it. <br /> <br /> <br /> So Yeah, lot's of Dark Ages books. I'm running Giovanni Chronicles and Transylvania Chronicles, besides a Byzantine solo-player game. <br /> And when my group play modern era Masquerade, We play South America, so I mostly read By Night books of the era for inspiration and structure, not for use. <br /> <br /> But I agree that the Chicago By Night are very well realised, and for good or bad, sticked as the default way of Camarilla princedoms (which for me isn't that bad, Camarilla is supposed to be a sect after all, so a reproduciable structure only makes sense).<br /> And that LA did the same, only mostly just bad, for the Anarchs. Besides, calling a little weak prince toppling a Second Anarch Revolt is a joke. The first one was a wave of consequence, that popped in many (entire) regions and became a continent-wide matter. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>New York By</b> Night failed to catch my attention, and I only looked into it after I played the Visual novel games. <br /> The <b>Montreal </b>and<b> Milwauke By Night</b> are very interesting in their ways, and give new ideas to the table each, even if some plots are ... unsavory. The Sabbat feels well-realized in them.<br /> <br /> I didn't read much (I could only read what I translated in google) of the <b>Frankfurt By Night </b>(Rheinesgold), but it also felt like a unique take on vampire politics. While I think Frederick first of all shouldn't be Barbarosa, and even more so, shouldn't be the most proggresive vampire in all Camarilla (he should be at least Brujah), his policies are very different from all other princes and turn Frankfurt into a very different place. Angiwar's stuff is also very cool. Frankfurt and Berlin should butt heads more.<br /> <br /> <b>Cairo By Night </b>has interesting ideas and political layout, but it could've gone deeper, or been more clear in some parts. I find it a fun resource, and think that it should've been more important in the metaplot, but alas it has been left in the dust. It does fill like the double-layered style city of ancient powers fighting age-old wars, while newer vampires are having their own struggles that indirectly suffer the effects of the War of Ages. What I hate though is the cover, I just don't understand what the hell is going on in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:46:37-07:00","id":1544135,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages Constanople by Night, Cult Of The Blood Gods, Players Guide, Dark Ages Iberia and Chicago by Night 5th edition.<br /> <br /> Ones I didn't care for all that much was New York By Night, Fall Of London, Blood Sigils, the most recent Camarilla and Sabbat sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> As for city building in general, Most of the time we use google to print off maps of a real life city and get a general idea which are the wealthy districts and the unsafe ones and go with nearby cities in our game. I don't think that there is a magical formula for city creation in the WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-17-2024, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T16:52:30-07:00","id":1544154,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of New Orleans by Night, but that's because its familiar, and home. I'm sure many people who live around Chicago, New York, and other cities feel the same way about their home turf.<br /> <br /> I feel the original Los Angelos by Night had a lot of potential for future updating with the groups and kindred show cased then, but every bit of media since has basically ignored their existence entirely. Where are you Christopher Haughton? :&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T18:14:33-07:00","id":1544165,"title":"","content":"I've actually been paying a lot of attention to the &quot;by Night&quot; books as part of a research project I was doing about representation in VtM. I don't have anything close to ready to say on the matter yet, but I do have some opinions. I think <i>Damnation City</i> for VtR is a better city book than any &quot;by Night&quot; book because it is more of a toolkit and guide to building cities and not a catalog of cool Kindred, but I digress.<br /> <br /> The first and second editions of <i>Chicago by Night</i> are understandably beloved because Chicago was the closest thing to a &quot;default setting&quot; that VtM had, particularly since the sample Gary chronicle from the first two core rulebooks tended to push games across the border. The Menele-Helena conflict set up the Jyhad as the primary driver of history and conflict. I know as a young storyteller back in 92-93, when Vampire was the game du jour among my friends, it encouraged a lot of metaplot that didn't give a lot of agency to the players. Second edition, by blowing up Chicago, attempted to create an instability that gave characters more room to breathe. Personally, I don't think it was successful because there are so goddamn many powerful Kindred running around the city, it was still hard for players to be the main characters of the story. I actually think the 5th Edition Chicago series (CbN5, <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i>, and <i>Chicago Folios</i>) did a decent job of opening up the city and making more room for the players, certainly a better job than CbN2.<br /> <br /> All of that said, one of the things that I think many of the later city books struggle with, and a lot of chronicles struggle with as well, is capturing the essence of a city. Instead, they focus on the Kindred as they interact in the Kindred society that developed over the 13/14 years of VtM's main production run. <i>Milwaukee by Night</i> and <i>L.A. by Night</i> at least tried to make the vibes different, even if they didn't perfectly capture the essence of the city.<br /> <br /> <i>New York by Night</i> was the most disappointing for me, probably because New York is the city I grew up in the shadow of, went to grad school in, and generally love the most. The vibrancy of the United States' largest and most diverse city was ignored for a focus on the runaway train that was VtM metaplot. It captured the zeitgeist of late-stage Vampire, but the characters and plot really could be placed anywhere and, for me, that is the wrong answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T07:27:40-07:00","id":1544200,"title":"","content":"Top<br /> <br /> Costantinople by Night<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night V5<br /> <br /> Transylvania by Night<br /> <br /> Montreal by Night<br /> <br /> France by Night<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mid<br /> <br /> Iberia by Night<br /> <br /> D.C. by Night<br /> <br /> New York by Night<br /> <br /> Fall of London<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bLos Angeles by Night<br /> <br /> Cairo by Night<br /> <br /> <br /> Bad<br /> <br /> Damascus by Night<br /> <br /> Dark Colony New England<br /> <br /> Mexico City by Night<br /> <br /> New Orleans by Night<br /> <br /> <br /> Worst<br /> <br /> Berlin by Night, despite the awesome concept<br /> <br /> <br /> Not city book but good books: House of Tremere, Dark Age Europe, Lair of the Hidden<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-18-2024, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T07:55:40-07:00","id":1544202,"title":"","content":"I'll separate in two categories :<ul><li><b>Modern </b>: definitely &quot;Montreal by Night&quot; (I'm a sabbat afficionado GM and player, and I do love the bizarre and religious undertones of it), and a bit of &quot;NY by Night&quot;.</li> <li><b>Dark Ages</b> : &quot;France by Night&quot; by far (it does help to be french ^^), and &quot;Constantinople by Night&quot; or &quot;Transylvania by Night&quot; in second position (mostly because of the cast of NPC for both).</li> <li>Not VtM, but too good to pass : &quot;Damnation City&quot; for VtR. This book served me far more for VtM than it did for it's own IP.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:46:32-07:00","id":1544219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544005#post1544005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. This is my most unique take but I\u2019ve got a special fondness for DC by Night. It was one of my first WoD books and I\u2019m from the DC metropolitan area so I\u2019ve got a fondness for the city (it\u2019s far more than just Capital Hill!). The cover is iconic (even if only to me) and makes wonderful use of the Washington monument (or, as I called it as a kid, \u2018the big pencil\u2019) as a gothic landmark. Now that said it\u2019s not perfect. Marcus Vitel is a somewhat gonzo concept but his long lasting popularity speaks for itself. Other than him and his brood though, the rest of the city\u2019s vampires are somewhat shaky. Lots of potential though.</div> </div> </div> </div>How interesting. I too, as a Washingtonian by birth, have a special fondness for DC by night. Peep my forum handle if you don't believe me.<br /> <br /> First, let me say that I don't think its unusual for a native of a region depicted in a &quot;By Night&quot; or &quot;Rage Across&quot; book to have, shall we say, <i>pointed</i> opinions on its portrayal. It doesn't seem there was any sort of requirement for the writer to have lived in the region for any length of time. And, to be fair, most of these were written before Wikipedia was a thing (or at least widely used). But I still feel like, despite some big hits, DC by Night had several problems.<br /> <br /> The Geography section reads like a tourist guide, with far too much attention on the various federal buildings but far too little attention to the neighborhoods where people actually live. The history section is phenomenal from the Colonial period up through the civil war. After that his interest in, ya know, the actual city of Washington DC seems to have waned. They misses out on a lot of the cities development as a center of (particularly African American) cultural expression and political struggle.<br /> <br /> I don't want to imply the author is, like committing a racism or something. But such disinterest in the cities actual residents has knock on effects elsewhere in the quality of the final product. Simply put, next time I wouldn't have someone from Mechanicsburg VA (300 miles away) write a book about Washington DC.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the fact it skips out on the cities diverse cultural history is made evident by the fact so few of the Vampires feel particularly tied to or part of the city. They are, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> put it, &quot;shaky&quot;. Most of them are broad enough vampiric stereotypes they could be slotted into almost any generic fictional ST created city. Ballet dancer Toreador. Serial Killer Malkavian. Drug runner Settite. Le yawn! Even Monica and Cynthia black are just kinda...there.<br /> <br /> No former intelligence agency Nossies? No Toreador with connection with any sort of black cultural product or era from the Chitlins Cricut through to Go-Go Music? No Brujah with any appreciable politics? In DC?!<br /> <br /> That (Malkavian? Ventrue?) chilling in the suburbs pretending to be Bela Legosi because he knows Vitel's secret and wants to be under-estimated was a good one, though. We needed more like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:52:34-07:00","id":1544220,"title":"","content":"Hi, I\u2019m not sure if this is relevant to the thread, but what if we include fan-made By Night books that are on the Storytellers Vault?<br /> <br /> What\u2019s your opinion? Are there any that are particularly valuable or interesting?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T14:45:35-07:00","id":1544234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544081#post1544081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Requiem's Shadows over Mexico book (also developed by Justin) specifically states that it was aiming for the sort of lurid sensationalism of various films and pop culture rather than any kind of realism, it wouldn't shock me if he had insisted on London by Night being the same. This would also be in line with some of the Dark Ages material like Transylvania by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could believe that of <i>London by Night</i> it it leaned into stereotypes, or played up Victorian melodrama, or something. But it's bland and uninspired, and doesn't have any sense of vision at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T15:08:11-07:00","id":1544236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544128#post1544128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Transylvania By Night</b> is... cool, but it is spread WAY too thin. We have an entire book trying to cover with detail 1/3 of Europe and going only by single characters, instead of structures or societies. And for a book about &quot;Tzimisce land&quot; we get very little Tzimisce in comparison. Almost no Voivodes, surely no content for how the Voivodates work, or examples of Knezes. So cool ideas, but too pulverized for my liking, focusing on characters that many times are unrelated (which should be the basis of any By Night). Showing the Balkans, or just Hungary and Romania should've been more than enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would broadly agree with this; they should have dropped Russia, Poland and Lithuania, maybe also Bohemia, and focused on Hungary, Bulgaria, and maybe Serbia and Bosnia. I mean, Bosnia was a centre of heterodox Christianity at the time (i.e. what most Christians would have regarded as heresy) so very thematically in keeping with the book. Still, I would argue that there is a lot of quality writing in the book, which is enough to keep it in my top tier for these types of supplements. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544128#post1544128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Iberia By Night</b> I thought was hot garbage. It should've been one of the most interesting regions, with Brujah, Toreador, Lasombra and Banu Haqim politics going wild. But it mostly is &quot;Muslisms are Haquimites&quot; and &quot;Christians are Lasombra&quot;, period. There are no freaking Brujah characters to speak of (and even worst, they stick a damn Ventrue as a great general for the Lasombra, out of nowhere), and Toreador basically a passing fad. No plots , just Amicti Noctis deciding &quot;ok, we'll go full-Christian&quot;, and no Banu Haqim putting the Laws of Haqim first (like Ur-Shulgi would many centuries later). There is no theme, no struggle, dilemma or campaign to take part in. It would just turn into War board game, which isn't functional for Vampire (just try the third chapter of Under the Black Cross to see how vampire open-war is very unfun to play). Besides, lots of important Lasombra characters aren't even in the book (like Eliser de Polanco and Tercio Bravo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, my regard for the book is slightly higher than yours ... but I'm not going to argue against any of these criticisms. There's this weird way of thinking in some of these supplements that a Muslim army conquers a region and, all of a sudden, all the vampires become Muslim, and then you have the inevitable conflict between Assamites and others. This appears implicitly in <i>Iberia by Night</i>. It's one of the books that lacks coherence because it had too many uncoordinated writers. If you look at the writing credits, you'll see that one writer's primary contribution was writing the Lasombra characters. Just the Lasombra characters.<br /> <br /> The sections on geography are very good, though. Compare how locations are handled here to the far inferior approach in <i>Dark Ages: British Isles</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544128#post1544128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Damascus By Night</b> I agree that is really underwhelming. Nothing in it justifies using Damascus, nor it has anything to do with Ashirra. The plot could've been in any city, and at any era nonetheless. For a book about Ashirra it has very little to do with it, and it does not use a venerable and great city like Damascus with any propriety. It's just the old plot of &quot;degenerate Elder is actually a puppet of a Baali&quot;, which I tire heavily every single time I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a complex one; the Baali originate in Syria, and there's potentially a good set up here, with the notion in Cainite society that the Baali are long defeated and marginalized, whereas they actually hold considerable power within one of the most important cities in Syria. There are two problems, though. The first is that this is a concept that requires a lot of development (and word count) to come across as more than a generic set up, which is something that isn't going to be achieved in a single chapter of a book. The second is that <i>Veil of Night</i> is a book primarily about Islam and the Ashirra, and, if you are going to spend a chapter on a city, it should be a chapter that reinforces and enhances the concepts in the rest of the book. Had Veil of Night included a chapter called, for, <i>Aleppo by Night</i>, which focused on the nature of an Ashirra domain, whilst we had <i>Damascus by Night</i> as a separate, full-length book, I think people's opinions may have been higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T00:20:21-07:00","id":1544262,"title":"","content":"Montreal By Night stands out in my mind as a favorite, while still having brutal flaws. Metathiax should have been a W:tA antagonist, and the byzantine plot surrounding the demon and the two body-swapped Cainites take up an awful lot of word count for a secret that's never going to impact players or their stories. That's space that could have better served the stated themes and tone if it had been spent on, say, storyteller tips on using the Sabbat Inquisition as antagonists or allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T08:58:40-07:00","id":1544293,"title":"","content":"Here's my official rankings of the modern-era &quot;By Night&quot; books<br /> <br /> <b>S Tier</b><br /> Chicago By Night 1st Edition<br /> Montreal By Night<br /> <br /> <b>A Tier</b><br /> Milwaukee By Night<br /> Alien Hunger<br /> Dark Colony<br /> <br /> <b>B Tier</b><br /> LA By Night<br /> DC By Night<br /> Berlin By Night (Fuck you, I liked it!)<br /> <br /> <b>C Tier</b><br /> New Orleans By Night<br /> Chicago By Night Second Edition<br /> Dark Alliance: Vancouver<br /> Blood Nativity (this would've been higher if there was just a little more details about Cleveland)<br /> <br /> <b>D Tier</b><br /> Cairo By Night<br /> Mexico City By Night<br /> New York By Night<br /> <br /> <b>F Tier</b><br /> Chicago By Night 5th Edition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T16:40:21-07:00","id":1544318,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, does anyone have a city they wish had been the subject of a by Night book?<br /> <br /> I always thought Dallas could have been potentially interesting, especially if it had leaned into the idea of Vampire doing some kind of neo-noir western thing.<br /> <br /> Miami also could have been a lot of fun, but I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen so that probably colors my opinion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T16:53:51-07:00","id":1544319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544318#post1544318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone have a city they wish had been the subject of a by Night book?<br /> <br /> I always thought Dallas could have been potentially interesting, especially if it had leaned into the idea of Vampire doing some kind of neo-noir western thing.<br /> <br /> Miami also could have been a lot of fun, but I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen so that probably colors my opinion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dallas By Night and Miami By Night would've been amazing, as would a Second Edition-era version of New York by Night<br /> <br /> Here's some of my picks for cities I would've loved to have seen get a &quot;By Night&quot; book...<br /> <br /> <b>North America</b><br /> Phoenix, Arizona<br /> Salt Lake City, Utah<br /> Seattle, Washington (tbh, I'm surprised this one didn't happen)<br /> El Paso, Texas<br /> Richmond, Virginia<br /> Charlotte, North Carolina<br /> Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania<br /> Calgary, Alberta<br /> Halifax, Nova Scotia<br /> Monterrey, Nuevo Leon<br /> Tijuana, Baja California<br /> <br /> <b>Europe</b><br /> Dublin, Ireland<br /> Manchester, England<br /> Lyon, France<br /> Cologne, Germany<br /> Saint Petersburg, Russia<br /> Athens, Greece<br /> Naples, Italy<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:04:58-07:00","id":1544322,"title":"","content":"Philadelphia getting skipped despite it's prominence in US history and still being a major city today has always kinda baffled me.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the lack of international cities in modern times books has always felt like a massive miss to me... though it's also clear that oWW didn't have the resources to do those cities justice in a fashion that would hold up with time. I do get the focus on North America because of the target audience, but it's still pretty strange how many major global cities never got any serious attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T20:02:47-07:00","id":1544335,"title":"","content":"Paris would have been potentially fascinating. I used to have an issue of National Geographic about the city's underground infrastructure, including things like medieval quarries that simply got covered up as the city grew, and it struck me as the kind of place that you could hide a <i>lot</i> of vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T11:45:15-07:00","id":1544349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544335#post1544335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paris would have been potentially fascinating. I used to have an issue of National Geographic about the city's underground infrastructure, including things like medieval quarries that simply got covered up as the city grew, and it struck me as the kind of place that you could hide a <i>lot</i> of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have loved a contemporary By Night treatment for one italian city: either Rome, Venice, Naples, Milan or Turin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T11:52:43-07:00","id":1544350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544319#post1544319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Europe</b><br /> Dublin, Ireland<br /> Manchester, England<br /> Lyon, France<br /> Cologne, Germany<br /> Saint Petersburg, Russia<br /> Athens, Greece<br /> Naples, Italy</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a European these would all be quite interesting cities to explore. I'd quite like to see focuses on cities which are key to either mortal or vampiric politics in a particular region, especially ones with long histories. For the UK I would quite like to see books or significant chapters on Cardiff, Edinburgh, Birmingham and York as well. As mentioned above Paris is an excellent location with a *lot* of really interesting elements to explore, I'd love to see more for say Budapest, Cordoba, Florence, Seville, Vienna to name just a few. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T14:29:23-07:00","id":1544358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544318#post1544318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought Dallas could have been potentially interesting, especially if it had leaned into the idea of Vampire doing some kind of neo-noir western thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe originally Steve Jackson Games intended to do a Dallas By Night back when they were doing GURPS versions of the World of Darkness, but that all fell apart when SJG got tired of what they considered excessive editing and changing of minds by White Wolf in approving content.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T17:42:21-07:00","id":1544365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544358#post1544358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe originally Steve Jackson Games intended to do a Dallas By Night back when they were doing GURPS versions of the World of Darkness, but that all fell apart when SJG got tired of what they considered excessive editing and changing of minds by White Wolf in approving content.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is something quite fascinating about books which never got into print. The original <i>San Francisco by Night </i>was due for publication in 1992, ten years before the (terrible) final version. In the early <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> books there were a lot of references to San Francisco, effectively trailing the publication. <br /> <br /> The other location sourcebook which didn't make it into print was <i>Rio by Night</i>; this one is a bit more murky, but was talked about a little in the mid-1990s, and would have been a book for second edition <i>Vampire</i>. It was even mentioned in the White Wolf writing / pitching guide at one point. <br /> <br /> (The other location sourcebook purportedly in development and which ended up never making it to print was <i>Rage Across India</i> for <i>Werewolf the Apocalypse</i>. Possibly a good thing...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T23:10:05-07:00","id":1544376,"title":"","content":"Would anyone be up for a NaNoWriMo challenge? One of the upsides about the modern gaming landscape is that, if we create material, we can easily bring it to a wider audience, and earn a return at the same time (via the Storytellers Vault in this instance). The NaNoWriMo target of 50,000 words in November would be a substantial portion of a book at the very least, and it's an opportunity to harness the community to fill in some blanks in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T04:53:25-07:00","id":1544385,"title":"","content":"Every one forgot Chaos Factory (Mexico by night 1\u00b0 edition? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T12:43:47-07:00","id":1544420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544319#post1544319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dallas By Night and Miami By Night would've been amazing, as would a Second Edition-era version of New York by Night<br /> <br /> Here's some of my picks for cities I would've loved to have seen get a &quot;By Night&quot; book...<br /> <br /> <b>North America</b><br /> Phoenix, Arizona<br /> Salt Lake City, Utah<br /> Seattle, Washington (tbh, I'm surprised this one didn't happen)<br /> El Paso, Texas<br /> Richmond, Virginia<br /> Charlotte, North Carolina<br /> Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania<br /> Calgary, Alberta<br /> Halifax, Nova Scotia<br /> Monterrey, Nuevo Leon<br /> Tijuana, Baja California<br /> <br /> <b>Europe</b><br /> Dublin, Ireland<br /> Manchester, England<br /> Lyon, France<br /> Cologne, Germany<br /> Saint Petersburg, Russia<br /> Athens, Greece<br /> Naples, Italy</div> </div> </div> </div>Ireland got a tiny mention/write up in Midnight Siege. Apparently there was some supernatural thing going on there and the Cammarilla abandoned their holdings to let the Sabbat take over and get wiped out by the problem supernatural thing.<br /> <br /> Anything Russia was covered mostly in Werewolf books because of the whole story with Baba Yaga and the Shadow Curtain. Besides Russia is part of Asia not Europe.<br /> <br /> I wish V20 would have gotten around to a Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom type bookline with the Drowned Legacies and South American cities. Rage Across the Amazon was the closest thing we got.<br /> <br /> Though I will say don't forget that some places did get a mention and information written about in the World of Darkness source books for both First and Second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:20:28-07:00","id":1544423,"title":"","content":"As I'm Canadian myself.<br /> <br /> Some of the following cities I would love to see the treatment.<br /> <br /> Calgary, Alberta: We use this city in our game as it's so close by.<br /> <br /> Winnipeg, Manitoba: one of the older cities outside of Ontario &amp; Quebec.<br /> <br /> Ottawa, Ontario is our Captail and I can see how the Camarilla, Sabbat and Anarchs wanting to have a foothold there.<br /> <br /> In the United States<br /> <br /> Detriot, Michigan. Has this city ever been touched by WOD?<br /> <br /> St. Paul, Minessota: I'm a big fan of the John Sanford series of novels that take place in that state","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:51:28-07:00","id":1544427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544423#post1544423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Detriot, Michigan. Has this city ever been touched by WOD?<br /> <br /> St. Paul, Minessota: I'm a big fan of the John Sanford series of novels that take place in that state</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Chronicles of Darkness's Promethean covering Detroit but not anything from WoD. If Hunter the Reckoning had done location books, I always thought that &quot;Hunting Ground: Detroit&quot; would have been a pretty good setting. It also would have made an interesting by Night book, with it as the more stereotypical Sabbat city in contrast to Montreal as the more esoteric one.<br /> <br /> Also, given how heavily 1st edition Vampire focused on the Midwest, I feel there must be some alternate universe in which the other games continued this trend, with Werewolf's signature setting being Rage Across Michigan and Mage's being the Twin Cities. (Changeling would have gotten Toronto; Wraith probably Cleveland.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T16:59:22-07:00","id":1544441,"title":"","content":"I always thought that a follow-up for Transylvania By Night (specially if it focused on Hungary and Romania) would be excellent, but other than Dark Ages Europe we never got anything. And I imagine it mostly because Transylvania Chronicles is considered as &quot;covering&quot; it. Which it really doesn't...<br /> <br /> A Rome By Night besides the Dark Ages Companion, which I thought it useful but a bit weak, would be cool. Be it modern or dark ages.<br /> Alexandria By Night would also be cool! There is/were Ravnos, Setite, Dastur Anosh, and lots of other interesting figures.<br /> <br /> An Ashirra city By Night would be awesome! We need a Chicago By Night for Ashirra.<br /> <br /> For my own country, I would love a Macei\u00f3 or Bahia By Night. Even a Bras\u00edlia By Night, in the vibe of a DC By Night would be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T09:25:45-07:00","id":1544468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544088#post1544088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion, but I actually like having historical and cultural figures as NPC's in these &quot;By Night&quot; books, it adds a certain pulpy charm to it all.<br /> <br /> Fuck, the greatest VTM setting book of all time was chock full of them. Chicago by Night had the likes of Al Capone, Harry Houdini, Mrs. O'Leary, Wat Tyler's girlfriend, and like a quarter of the cast of the friggin' Iliad as elder vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case besides Doc Holliday inspired npc in our series, maybe I can get the gm to bring in some of the Earps or Johnny Ringo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:07:10-07:00","id":1544506,"title":"","content":"I'd love to have had Barcelona by Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T19:33:46-07:00","id":1544525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544506#post1544506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to have had Barcelona by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some really intriguing concepts of Barcelona in the original A World of Darkness (1992). A city book that did the city's history right and utilized those concepts would be very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T14:13:18-07:00","id":1544592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544427#post1544427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember Chronicles of Darkness's Promethean covering Detroit but not anything from WoD. If Hunter the Reckoning had done location books, I always thought that &quot;Hunting Ground: Detroit&quot; would have been a pretty good setting. It also would have made an interesting by Night book, with it as the more stereotypical Sabbat city in contrast to Montreal as the more esoteric one.<br /> <br /> Also, given how heavily 1st edition Vampire focused on the Midwest, I feel there must be some alternate universe in which the other games continued this trend, with Werewolf's signature setting being Rage Across Michigan and Mage's being the Twin Cities. (Changeling would have gotten Toronto; Wraith probably Cleveland.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that Promethean The Created did have a section on Detriot as did Changeling The Lost made a mention of it being a Freehold controlled by the Winter &amp; Spring Courts, but I was thinking was it ever touched upon the older games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T14:44:25-07:00","id":1544594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544318#post1544318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone have a city they wish had been the subject of a by Night book?<br /> <br /> I always thought Dallas could have been potentially interesting, especially if it had leaned into the idea of Vampire doing some kind of neo-noir western thing.<br /> <br /> Miami also could have been a lot of fun, but I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen so that probably colors my opinion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I wouldn't be able to list them all even if I wanted to. It's funny there are literally more city books about US cities than in whole Europe, when to vampires it's a bit obvious that Europe would be much more important than the USA. <br /> <br /> Just to make a short list:<br /> <br /> Nuremberg, Germany<br /> Dresden, Germany<br /> Munich, Germany<br /> Hamburg, Germany<br /> Florence, Italy<br /> Genoa, Italy<br /> Venice, Italy<br /> Barcelona, Spain<br /> Prag, Tschechien<br /> Edinburg, Schottland<br /> Dublin, Ireland<br /> <br /> The list could go on for quite a while...but it's a shame these weren't...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T16:40:05-07:00","id":1544601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544594#post1544594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I wouldn't be able to list them all even if I wanted to. It's funny there are literally more city books about US cities than in whole Europe, when to vampires it's a bit obvious that Europe would be much more important than the USA.<br /> <br /> Just to make a short list:<br /> <br /> Nuremberg, Germany<br /> Dresden, Germany<br /> Munich, Germany<br /> Hamburg, Germany<br /> Florence, Italy<br /> Genoa, Italy<br /> Venice, Italy<br /> Barcelona, Spain<br /> Prag, Tschechien<br /> Edinburg, Schottland<br /> Dublin, Ireland<br /> <br /> The list could go on for quite a while...but it's a shame these weren't...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that White Wolf was an American company, and, initially, were almost exclusively selling to an American audience, which obviously shaped their publication choices. There was also a specific in-game reason for concentrating on America, which was that, in the early editions, Europe was portrayed as a stable region, dominated by elders, whilst America was dynamic and riven by conflict. This characterisation had largely receded by revised, but was certainly there initially.<br /> <br /> And ... it's fine saying that certain cities ought to have books devoted to them, but these books need to have a reason to exist in terms of their contents. So, take a notional <i>Hamburg by Night</i>, for instance. What's so interesting about the city in terms of the World of Darkness which would make it a compelling place to write about? Or Dresden? And, whilst, in reality, it's not too hard to create one or two interesting hooks, as a publisher you may well run out of steam quite quickly. You also have to sell these books to people. A sourcebook devoted to a key city which is supposed to exemplify the setting, like Chicago, is not too bad. But, as a publisher, you also have to justify why a potential purchaser might want to buy not just <i>Chicago by Night</i>, but also <i>Detroit by Night</i>, <i>Indianapolis by Night</i>, and <i>St Louis by Night</i>, which are at least in the vicinity of Chicago, and can therefore be used directly in a chronicle set in Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:20:44-07:00","id":1544614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544376#post1544376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone be up for a NaNoWriMo challenge? One of the upsides about the modern gaming landscape is that, if we create material, we can easily bring it to a wider audience, and earn a return at the same time (via the Storytellers Vault in this instance). The NaNoWriMo target of 50,000 words in November would be a substantial portion of a book at the very least, and it's an opportunity to harness the community to fill in some blanks in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did DriveThru's Next Adventure Game Jam in September (ironically, a VtM product) and that was hard as hell for me to stay on track. I salute those of you who can successfully stay at it for a straight month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:24:30-07:00","id":1544615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544441#post1544441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Rome By Night besides the Dark Ages Companion, which I thought it useful but a bit weak, would be cool. Be it modern or dark ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rome might be an interesting three-piece project, with Roman Republic/Empire, Dark Ages, and Modern Nights versions to compare and contrast the changes over the centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Ashirra city By Night would be awesome! We need a Chicago By Night for Ashirra. </div> </div> </div>I have only glanced over it a little bit but doesn't <i>Cairo by Night</i> do that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T20:41:54-07:00","id":1544622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544601#post1544601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And ... it's fine saying that certain cities ought to have books devoted to them, but these books need to have a reason to exist in terms of their contents.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone that doesn't see a lot of inherent value in any of these books, I don't find it that compelling to demand too much of a bar for more of them. People like them. If people like them, and people buy them, then there's no real other reason for companies to make them. One of the reasons for wider ranging books geographically is to allow more variety to them and thus keep things fresh.<br /> <br /> Additionally, it's not inherently a bad idea to encourage people to broaden their horizons a bit. The books have to be compelling, but there's a certain value it taking a city your target audience wouldn't immediately think of and showing how any city can be something special with some research and creative presentation.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, take a notional <i>Hamburg by Night</i>, for instance. What's so interesting about the city in terms of the World of Darkness which would make it a compelling place to write about? Or Dresden? </div> </div> </div>Hamburg is an industrial powerhouse (it's the largest port city in Germany, and one of the largest in Europe) with history as a trade center going back to the Holy Roman Empire, making it a natural vampire hub for influence over power. Not just in Germany, but in the EU and even globally as Hamburg is home to a number of institutes that work on international trade law and frequently it hosts UN/etc. meetings on such topics.<br /> <br /> Hamburg is also one of Europe's largest centers of journalism, making it an essential place for vampires to vie for control to keep the Masquerade intact. The large number of UNESCO heritage sites is also a nice bit of fun for vampires that want their homes to be maintained for generations.<br /> <br /> Hamburg might not be my first choice for a German city... but if it's not in your top 5... you probably know very little about modern Germany or it's history.<br /> <br /> Dresden could be a bit repetitive, but frankly it has such a strong hook as a Vampire/Wraith crossover book after the Allied destruction of it that exploring the supernatural repercussions of the firebombing is more than enough of a hook to carry a book on top of Dresden's unique history as a major German city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T21:44:46-07:00","id":1544625,"title":"","content":"The only By Night book I read was Chicago; I found it interesting, but. not enough for me to have any interest in reading the other By-Night books. I prefer to create my own cities with my own NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T22:16:07-07:00","id":1544626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544622#post1544622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone that doesn't see a lot of inherent value in any of these books, I don't find it that compelling to demand too much of a bar for more of them. People like them. If people like them, and people buy them, then there's no real other reason for companies to make them. One of the reasons for wider ranging books geographically is to allow more variety to them and thus keep things fresh.<br /> <br /> Additionally, it's not inherently a bad idea to encourage people to broaden their horizons a bit. The books have to be compelling, but there's a certain value it taking a city your target audience wouldn't immediately think of and showing how any city can be something special with some research and creative presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as you don't see the inherent value in these books, you're not understanding the problems found within producing them either. This isn't, for instance, travel writing; there's nothing wrong with broadening the horizons of your audience, but this shouldn't ever going to be the primary motivation behind creating a location sourcebook for a game. So, if we take the first edition of <i>Chicago by Night</i>, we have a book ostensibly about Chicago, whilst actually being about obtaining and exercising power, the blurring of history and literature, and an epic and almost concealed struggle within the World of Darkness. The book was very intentionally designed to explain how <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> worked on a &quot;show not tell&quot; basis, taking the reader through various power levels, right back to a pair of Methuselahs caught up in a two-thousand-year conflict. It had a very clear reason for existing, which is why it met with critical acclaim.<br /> <br /> Now, compare this with <i>London by Night</i>, which existed because someone thought it was about time for a London sourcebook, and was written by a team of authors who seem to have no great interest in either London or the Victorian period. <br /> <br /> Now, leaving aside opportunity costs in publishing (which is actually a massive issue if you want to make a profit), books exist, or at least ought to exist, for a reason. If you want to create (for instance) an equivalent to <i>Chicago by Night</i>, you, as the author, need to have something to say, and some greater insights than &quot;this place exists and is kind of cool&quot;. The latter thinking is what led us to most of the worst location sourcebooks which have been published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T02:47:48-07:00","id":1544636,"title":"","content":"I think the correlation of intent and end result is.... questionable. Given how much New Orleans mattered personally to some of the oWW staff, and the book set there had something to say, it's also a joke of a book because they still put a subway, in New Orleans.<br /> <br /> There's nothing unique about Chicago that makes CbN special. You could do what it did in almost any major city in the world (some of it might have made more sense... the reasons why some of the older CbN NPCs are in Chicago of all places is... flimsy at best).<br /> <br /> The idea that Chicago is somehow superior than Hamburg for &quot;having a point&quot; doesn't really fly. Chicago got picked for reasons that aren't because Chicago was particularly special for the idea of &quot;showing how VtM works,&quot; or &quot;having something to say.&quot; It's just the biases of the people that made the picks. It doesn't really address that there's all sorts of stories that would benefit from being told outside of North America because other issues might be better in the contexts of other cultural landscapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T04:19:35-07:00","id":1544641,"title":"","content":"I suspect Chicago might've been picked as the signature city at least partially because of how much it appeared in film during the 1980s.<br /> <br /> Just on a personal level, one of the reasons I find it suitable as a potential Vampire signature city is just how much of a reputation for political corruption it had for most of the 20th century. (And yes, the same could be said for most major US cities, but for whatever weird reason, Chicago had just kind of developed that sort of public perception.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T04:23:22-07:00","id":1544642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544615#post1544615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rome might be an interesting three-piece project, with Roman Republic/Empire, Dark Ages, and Modern Nights versions to compare and contrast the changes over the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rennaissance era would have been cool too, but that probably would have been more suitable as a Mage: The Sorcerers Crusade thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T08:49:35-07:00","id":1544652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544636#post1544636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the correlation of intent and end result is.... questionable. Given how much New Orleans mattered personally to some of the oWW staff, and the book set there had something to say, it's also a joke of a book because they still put a subway, in New Orleans.<br /> <br /> There's nothing unique about Chicago that makes CbN special. You could do what it did in almost any major city in the world (some of it might have made more sense... the reasons why some of the older CbN NPCs are in Chicago of all places is... flimsy at best).<br /> <br /> The idea that Chicago is somehow superior than Hamburg for &quot;having a point&quot; doesn't really fly. Chicago got picked for reasons that aren't because Chicago was particularly special for the idea of &quot;showing how VtM works,&quot; or &quot;having something to say.&quot; It's just the biases of the people that made the picks. It doesn't really address that there's all sorts of stories that would benefit from being told outside of North America because other issues might be better in the contexts of other cultural landscapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I couldn't agree more with what you've said here. There's nothing inherently special about Chicago that made it a good book. It was the characters and stories that were put there and ofc they did a good job, but... it always felt &quot;flimsy at best&quot; as you put it, that many things and characters were there in the first place, as my childhood friend would jokingly say &quot;Ofc the alliens are always going to invade the USA as also naturally it only makes sense that two legendary characters from greek mythology would end up in the USA for a reason, ofc Daniel, everything must happen in America&quot; lol.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night is, as most Vampire books, character's driven and I'd even go as far as to say that it's likely one of the (if not the) main reasons people are interested in City Books, to see if they're going to find &quot;a Helena and Menelaus sort of story there&quot; or other interesting characters that could perhaps fill into another role or another place (that in this case would make a lot of sense lol) or serve as example for another character, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, take a notional <i>Hamburg by Night</i>, for instance. What's so interesting about the city in terms of the World of Darkness which would make it a compelling place to write about? </div> </div> </div>All things considered, Hamburg (now that we're talking abou this beautiful city) would have made a much more fitting city even for the two to be in, now that we're talking about Helena and Menelaus. The city has a long and rich history, it has a special relationship with the sea, was a very important member of the Hanseatic League, hell! just the Hanseatic League in itself makes it suberbly interesting in itself, be it a modern setting or for a dark ages game to explore, there are just so many things about Hamburg, I could go on here for quite a while, but I have work to do right now, anyway. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said it's just people's biases that made the choices or perhaps more simply put in these words:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's worth remembering that White Wolf was an American company, and, initially, were almost exclusively selling to an American audience, which obviously shaped their publication choices. </div> </div> </div>That's basically the only argument, besides people's biases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T09:29:12-07:00","id":1544655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544318#post1544318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone have a city they wish had been the subject of a by Night book?<br /> <br /> I always thought Dallas could have been potentially interesting, especially if it had leaned into the idea of Vampire doing some kind of neo-noir western thing.<br /> <br /> Miami also could have been a lot of fun, but I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen so that probably colors my opinion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Miami is an enormous missed opportunity. Not only is it a unique part of the country with centuries of cultural collisions under its belt in real life, it was also a firmly entrenched Sabbat city whose importance to the faction was based entirely on the east coast war effort. It would have been a natural locale for a look at the war through that faction's eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 11-04-2024, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T11:03:45-07:00","id":1544661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544615#post1544615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have only glanced over it a little bit but doesn't <i>Cairo by Night</i> do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not really in my view. Even mukhtar bey is called a Prince and not a Sultan, besides not having much of a feeling of an Ashirra structure. The sect shouldn't be Camarilla with Arab names. Cairo is more of a city of portents and big ancient powers working their schemes from the dark, whilist newer generations are making their (un)living none of the wiser. It has more of a Setite and Tal'Mahe'Ra going on than Ashirra. <br /> <br /> So I don't really see Cairo By Night being that, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T15:09:07-07:00","id":1544686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544636#post1544636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the correlation of intent and end result is.... questionable. Given how much New Orleans mattered personally to some of the oWW staff, and the book set there had something to say, it's also a joke of a book because they still put a subway, in New Orleans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you tell me what page of NObN had a subway listed? I'm reading through it and I see no such thing. New Orleans has always had quite a bit of rail traffic, as well as you can take a street car through most of the city for public transit.<br /> <br /> The worst offense the NObN book has, is that its part of the Samuel Haight meta plot stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T19:38:52-07:00","id":1544701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The worst offense the NObN book has, is that its part of the Samuel Haight meta plot stuff. </div> </div> </div>That's actually probably the best part lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T05:12:58-07:00","id":1544718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544701#post1544701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually probably the best part lol</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my point ;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T05:23:18-08:00","id":1545245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544601#post1544601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth remembering that White Wolf was an American company, and, initially, were almost exclusively selling to an American audience, which obviously shaped their publication choices. There was also a specific in-game reason for concentrating on America, which was that, in the early editions, Europe was portrayed as a stable region, dominated by elders, whilst America was dynamic and riven by conflict. This characterisation had largely receded by revised, but was certainly there initially.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While <i>North America</i> was portrayed as a land of conflict, a substantial amount of the conflict described in the city books took place outside the US proper. I wonder whose choice was it to set the first (V2) Sabbat city book in Montreal and not in, I don't know, Detroit or Miami. I don't think there was ever a<i> By Night </i>book devoted to any of the stated Sabbat bastions in the US, actually\u2014<i>Chicago</i> may just come the closest. Even <i>New York by Night</i> basically left out any mention of the city's tenure as a Sabbat stronghold, despite all the implications the most populous city in the US being outside Camarilla control for most of the 20th century has for.. everything, really.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I always wanted to see<i> Milan by Night</i>. There is literally no city in Italy less intuitive for a Sabbat bastion than Milan\u2014yet maybe, just maybe, they could've made it work. (Not that I ever liked the way Europe was characterised in these books; we've had more revolutions, wars and uprisings in the last two centuries than all of the Middle East. Portraying Europe as a static bastion of Elders just rubs me the wrong way.) That, or a <i>New York by Night</i> set during the 70s (which I've always imagined as the height of Sabbat control in the city). If the authors kept it tasteful, I feel like there's much inspiration to be found for a Sabbat chronicle in the Son of Sam murders.<br /> <br /> (That's all not mentioning how White Wolf has always harboured a certain fascination with the foreign, even though most of the early V:tM material was explicitly made with an American audience in mind. Starting with <i>Kindred of the East</i>...)<br /> <br /> * This message went through a couple of edits as I read your comment more carefully. I believe this will be the final version<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","user":"gamiem","date":". 11-03-2024, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T11:45:28-08:00","id":1545263,"title":"","content":"Cairo was an interesting book because of the age of the city and that a handful of potent and ancient kindred would be actively plotting against each other and seeing the Camarilla and Sabbat residing there in a tense truce of sorts is something that would be out of place in North America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T00:14:26-08:00","id":1545284,"title":"","content":"As an Aussie, I\u2019d love Sydney By Night. We\u2019ve had the brief mentions of Prince Sarrasine for so long, but nothing of any actual substance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T22:54:56-07:00","id":1549535,"title":"","content":"Best: Constantinople by Night, Montreal by Night<br /> <br /> Also liked New Orleans and Chicago. <br /> <br /> Worst- Berlin, they left so much to be desired and New York.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T09:42:51-07:00","id":1549540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1545245#post1545245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While <i>North America</i> was portrayed as a land of conflict, a substantial amount of the conflict described in the city books took place outside the US proper. I wonder whose choice was it to set the first (V2) Sabbat city book in Montreal and not in, I don't know, Detroit or Miami. I don't think there was ever a<i> By Night </i>book devoted to any of the stated Sabbat bastions in the US, actually\u2014<i>Chicago</i> may just come the closest. Even <i>New York by Night</i> basically left out any mention of the city's tenure as a Sabbat stronghold, despite all the implications the most populous city in the US being outside Camarilla control for most of the 20th century has for.. everything, really.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I always wanted to see<i> Milan by Night</i>. There is literally no city in Italy less intuitive for a Sabbat bastion than Milan\u2014yet maybe, just maybe, they could've made it work. (Not that I ever liked the way Europe was characterised in these books; we've had more revolutions, wars and uprisings in the last two centuries than all of the Middle East. Portraying Europe as a static bastion of Elders just rubs me the wrong way.) That, or a <i>New York by Night</i> set during the 70s (which I've always imagined as the height of Sabbat control in the city). If the authors kept it tasteful, I feel like there's much inspiration to be found for a Sabbat chronicle in the Son of Sam murders.<br /> <br /> (That's all not mentioning how White Wolf has always harboured a certain fascination with the foreign, even though most of the early V:tM material was explicitly made with an American audience in mind. Starting with <i>Kindred of the East</i>...)<br /> <br /> * This message went through a couple of edits as I read your comment more carefully. I believe this will be the final version<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all fairness, Vampire Europe is not daylight Europe and it actually says something interesting about the Camarilla for the Elders of the Ivory Tower to be standing tall after so many centuries of frequently-violent change (To quote an expert \u201cGovernments come and go, I do not\u201d), especially if one shows the combination of subtlety, stubbornness, luck and ruthlessness it took to achieve this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T03:46:21-07:00","id":1549552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1549540#post1549540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In all fairness, Vampire Europe is not daylight Europe and it actually says something interesting about the Camarilla for the Elders of the Ivory Tower to be standing tall after so many centuries of frequently-violent change (To quote an expert \u201cGovernments come and go, I do not\u201d), especially if one shows the combination of subtlety, stubbornness, luck and ruthlessness it took to achieve this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the stasis of Europe's vampiric society is difficult to separate from the game's unjustifiably parochial conviction Europe exists only as a kind of prelude to North America, which is where history proper is assumed to take place; hence why the vampiric history of Europe effectively stops at the Convention of Thorns. To be clear, even if one allows for Europe to exist as an independent historic unit from North America, I'd question the choice to have the continent's vampiric history (only) be told from the perspective of elders. If the site of modern-day Milan being continuously inhabited since Roman times is sufficient justification for the Prince of Milan in 1997 to literally be the same guy as the one who spearheaded the Milanese theatre of the Great Anarch Revolt\u2014even though just about the only thing modern Milan shares with its 15th century predecessor is the name\u2014why should events like the Spanish conquest of Tenochtitlan impact the vampiric history of Mesoamerica?<br /> <br /> (The answer is, of course, that the people behind V:tM see Europe as &quot;old&quot; in an absolute sense, and not simply older than North America\u2014and even then, only the part of it north of the Rio Grande)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","user":"gamiem","date":". 03-25-2025, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T12:17:24-07:00","id":1549561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1549552#post1549552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the stasis of Europe's vampiric society is difficult to separate from the game's unjustifiably parochial conviction Europe exists only as a kind of prelude to North America, which is where history proper is assumed to take place; hence why the vampiric history of Europe effectively stops at the Convention of Thorns. To be clear, even if one allows for Europe to exist as an independent historic unit from North America, I'd question the choice to have the continent's vampiric history (only) be told from the perspective of elders. If the site of modern-day Milan being continuously inhabited since Roman times is sufficient justification for the Prince of Milan in 1997 to literally be the same guy as the one who spearheaded the Milanese theatre of the Great Anarch Revolt\u2014even though just about the only thing modern Milan shares with its 15th century predecessor is the name\u2014why should events like the Spanish conquest of Tenochtitlan impact the vampiric history of Mesoamerica?<br /> <br /> (The answer is, of course, that the people behind V:tM see Europe as &quot;old&quot; in an absolute sense, and not simply older than North America\u2014and even then, only the part of it north of the Rio Grande)</div> </div> </div> </div> When it comes to that sort of question, I tend to say \u201cSome vampires rolled better than others\u201d and leave it there.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T09:17:48-07:00","id":1549672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543998-best-and-worst-by-night-vtm-and-vda?p=1544086#post1544086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it shows I was a bit distracted when writing this bit\u2026 But one of the nice things is that the book did have a sensible limited number of characters, so we didn\u2019t really end up with unnecessary filler.</div> </div> </div> </div>NOLA by Night is hands-down my favourite. It just has the right *mood*. It feels grounded. The relationships feel organic. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}